sbsigntool - Signing utility for UEFI secure boot

  Copyright (C) 2102 Jeremy Kerr <jeremy.kerr@canonical.com>
  Copyright (C) Emily <info@emy.sh>

  Copying and distribution of this file, with or without modification,
  are permitted in any medium without royalty provided the copyright
  notice and this notice are preserved.

Building requires CMake 3.20 or newer, a C compiler, OpenSSL, libuuid.
Manual pages require help2man. Tests additionally require the the openssl 
command, bash, objdump, and hexdump.

sbkeysync is automatically enabled when libefivar and compatible headers are found.
Otherwise, it is omitted without failing configuration.

Configure and build out of tree, then install:

  cmake -S . -B build
  cmake --build build
  cmake --install build

The install prefix can be set with -DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=/usr.
Use -DBUILD_TESTING=OFF to omit test support or -DBUILD_MAN_PAGES=OFF to
omit manuals.

To build and run the tests:

  cmake -S . -B build -DBUILD_TESTING=ON
  cmake --build build
  ctest --test-dir build --output-on-failure

CTest generates fresh test certificates before running the shell tests.
Installation is not required to run the tests.

sbsigntool is free software.  See the file COPYING for copying conditions.
